        ("p", r"The sign of a weight is the direction of the influence, its absolute value is the strength. A weight also carries units: if $x_i$ is a floor area in m² and $a$ is a price in thousands of dollars, then $w_i$ is measured in “thousands of dollars per m²”. Weights are the neuron’s memory: everything it has learned from the data is stored in them and in the bias."),

